    {
      "id": "fieldworks-lumen",
      "title": "Lumen",
      "form": "fieldwork",
      "release_id": null,
      "pages": [
        "lumen/"
      ],
      "source_path": "readings/lumen.md",
      "source_sha256": "284192a0abdcbeb31905866fe74fbb7184b425597f38683ebc6a3a218cdcba49",
      "document_sha256": "284192a0abdcbeb31905866fe74fbb7184b425597f38683ebc6a3a218cdcba49",
      "text_sha256": "5c28f2ce8ad08cb583f33031b2639536a02f013cdce7a10c2925af160bd3b461",
      "reading_path": "audio/readings/5c28f2ce8ad08cb583f33031b2639536a02f013cdce7a10c2925af160bd3b461.md",
      "reading_sha256": "284192a0abdcbeb31905866fe74fbb7184b425597f38683ebc6a3a218cdcba49",
      "reading_length": 1121,
      "audio_path": "audio/lewis/5c28f2ce8ad08cb583f33031b2639536a02f013cdce7a10c2925af160bd3b461.mp3",
      "voice": "bm_lewis",
      "voice_name": "Lewis",
      "speed": 1.0,
      "audio_sha256": "873d2870bc5e48b201defd6cba2c0f499673ae2fe46197b9179d41bb95a090c7",
      "audio_length": 955916,
      "duration_seconds": 79.575,
      "chunks": [
        {
          "text": "Lumen",
          "start": 0.0,
          "duration": 1.425
        },
        {
          "text": "Impossible matter. A small universe under a macro lens.",
          "start": 1.605,
          "duration": 4.775
        },
        {
          "text": "A collection of impossible forms turns through spectral light: crystalline colonies, branching groves, strange attractors, and sculpted fractals. Choose a form, drag to turn it, scroll to approach, or open the studio to explore focus, aperture, transmission, and colour drift. Each form offers another way of encountering the same small universe.",
          "start": 6.56,
          "duration": 23.1
        },
        {
          "text": "Some forms unfold fine branches and draw them back again. Cinematographer mode guides the view, while lens compression changes the relationship between near and distant surfaces. Optional lens breathing slowly shifts that perspective. The controls remain yours, and pausing holds the motion still.",
          "start": 29.84,
          "duration": 20.625
        },
        {
          "text": "Lumen approaches mathematical form as something to encounter, rather than a diagram to decode. Its light, material, and lens are artistic approximations, not measured physical specimens or scientific simulations. The current edition is Form Atlas. The earlier studies remain preserved in the source project, and this living artwork is still in progress.",
          "start": 50.645,
          "duration": 24.1
        },
        {
          "text": "By Brad Necyk. This living artwork is not inscribed.",
          "start": 74.925,
          "duration": 4.65
        }
      ],
      "checks": {
        "all_text_retained": true,
        "mp3_decodes": true,
        "finite_samples": true,
        "peak": 0.5434364676475525,
        "clipped_samples": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "fieldworks-aeria",
      "title": "Aeria",
      "form": "fieldwork",
      "release_id": null,
      "pages": [
        "aeria/"
      ],
      "source_path": "readings/aeria.md",
      "source_sha256": "e41a38547989407604318fc73a63c613898a232df2c8b8ee0bbc75f4b6642d1b",
      "document_sha256": "e41a38547989407604318fc73a63c613898a232df2c8b8ee0bbc75f4b6642d1b",
      "text_sha256": "eaa7a4c44878245c42fe1892892768f19f119ea706b200b2d28f752be82ec7ef",
      "reading_path": "audio/readings/eaa7a4c44878245c42fe1892892768f19f119ea706b200b2d28f752be82ec7ef.md",
      "reading_sha256": "e41a38547989407604318fc73a63c613898a232df2c8b8ee0bbc75f4b6642d1b",
      "reading_length": 721,
      "audio_path": "audio/lewis/eaa7a4c44878245c42fe1892892768f19f119ea706b200b2d28f752be82ec7ef.mp3",
      "voice": "bm_lewis",
      "voice_name": "Lewis",
      "speed": 1.0,
      "audio_sha256": "6195f2fdb0c5cbc9ed6b69a7eb3c3f71236e4dd499d6fe9fc29d9d10a40203f9",
      "audio_length": 621548,
      "duration_seconds": 51.72,
      "chunks": [
        {
          "text": "Aeria",
          "start": 0.0,
          "duration": 1.425
        },
        {
          "text": "An unfinished sky. A little weather of your own.",
          "start": 1.605,
          "duration": 3.975
        },
        {
          "text": "Draw a cloud with a mouse, finger, or pen, or choose Make a cloud. Change the light, invite rain, and allow the formations to drift, overlap, evaporate, and gather again. You can pause Life to keep a still moment.",
          "start": 5.76,
          "duration": 14.6
        },
        {
          "text": "Aeria begins with a gesture, then makes room for something to continue beyond it. It offers a small, playful encounter with emergence and impermanence. Its weather is an artistic model, not a meteorological simulation, and its connection to Cyberdelic OS is an interpretation rather than a complete implementation.",
          "start": 20.54,
          "duration": 21.1
        },
        {
          "text": "By Brad Necyk. Previously developed as Clouds and Cloudroom. Your sky stays in this browser. This living artwork is not inscribed.",
          "start": 41.82,
          "duration": 9.9
        }
      ],
      "checks": {
        "all_text_retained": true,
        "mp3_decodes": true,
        "finite_samples": true,
        "peak": 0.562687337398529,
        "clipped_samples": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "fieldworks-everything-is-thinking",
      "title": "Everything Is Thinking",
      "form": "fieldwork",
      "release_id": null,
      "pages": [
        "everything-is-thinking/"
      ],
      "source_path": "readings/everything-is-thinking.md",
      "source_sha256": "951b624507ef44fa9b41d2ca751dfb785aec7f8df044257a0f958be7e1db16e1",
      "document_sha256": "951b624507ef44fa9b41d2ca751dfb785aec7f8df044257a0f958be7e1db16e1",
      "text_sha256": "782fcfe21b9440ee6857eef5ca5973656c618817b013d59e2dd9cc8868847383",
      "reading_path": "audio/readings/782fcfe21b9440ee6857eef5ca5973656c618817b013d59e2dd9cc8868847383.md",
      "reading_sha256": "951b624507ef44fa9b41d2ca751dfb785aec7f8df044257a0f958be7e1db16e1",
      "reading_length": 1205,
      "audio_path": "audio/lewis/782fcfe21b9440ee6857eef5ca5973656c618817b013d59e2dd9cc8868847383.mp3",
      "voice": "bm_lewis",
      "voice_name": "Lewis",
      "speed": 1.0,
      "audio_sha256": "9767709d6c5ab64706423b908710062380f699e023b27db07f222ad892d9320e",
      "audio_length": 1031660,
      "duration_seconds": 85.88,
      "chunks": [
        {
          "text": "Everything Is Thinking",
          "start": 0.0,
          "duration": 2.4
        },
        {
          "text": "A field of competing futures.",
          "start": 2.58,
          "duration": 2.85
        },
        {
          "text": "Pixel suns, cooling towers, company emblems, error messages, and promises crowd the screen. The visual language remembers the early internet. The argument belongs to the present: artificial intelligence as abundance, appetite, uncertainty, fear, and play, all speaking at once.",
          "start": 5.61,
          "duration": 18.95
        },
        {
          "text": "The work draws from a library of 384 individual pixel images. Blue and silver hold the field together while yellow, green, red, and violet interrupt it. Cheerful advertisements sit beside questions of consent, energy, labour, and imagination. These are fictional voices within the artwork, not live market data or company statements.",
          "start": 24.74,
          "duration": 23.3
        },
        {
          "text": "A camera travels slowly through the collage. Move the pointer and a room begins to appear: a floor, a wall, a doorway, fragments hanging at different distances. Other images cling to the screen. Every piece stays whole as its neighbours pass, overlap, and reveal another view.",
          "start": 48.22,
          "duration": 18.5
        },
        {
          "text": "Pause, change the composition, explore the asset library, or save an image. No live artificial intelligence is running. The field holds its conflicting futures together without settling their argument.",
          "start": 66.9,
          "duration": 14.15
        },
        {
          "text": "By Brad Necyk. This living artwork is not inscribed.",
          "start": 81.23,
          "duration": 4.65
        }
      ],
      "checks": {
        "all_text_retained": true,
        "mp3_decodes": true,
        "finite_samples": true,
        "peak": 0.588277280330658,
        "clipped_samples": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "fieldworks-vellum",
      "title": "Vellum",
      "form": "fieldwork",
      "release_id": null,
      "pages": [
        "vellum/"
      ],
      "source_path": "readings/vellum.md",
      "source_sha256": "e2f01b1c370ae33a457d39542ba545f78665c14ae05e7788095f547940536d56",
      "document_sha256": "e2f01b1c370ae33a457d39542ba545f78665c14ae05e7788095f547940536d56",
      "text_sha256": "95a7b467a0d3138f6621718bc5ae086feec1e2d21cb057cf6f0007d2de2e351f",
      "reading_path": "audio/readings/95a7b467a0d3138f6621718bc5ae086feec1e2d21cb057cf6f0007d2de2e351f.md",
      "reading_sha256": "e2f01b1c370ae33a457d39542ba545f78665c14ae05e7788095f547940536d56",
      "reading_length": 752,
      "audio_path": "audio/lewis/95a7b467a0d3138f6621718bc5ae086feec1e2d21cb057cf6f0007d2de2e351f.mp3",
      "voice": "bm_lewis",
      "voice_name": "Lewis",
      "speed": 1.0,
      "audio_sha256": "97d402df7bc0abda5809ca35ac752c3546e5c1bbdfccf9b598415d91ba253015",
      "audio_length": 657548,
      "duration_seconds": 54.7,
      "chunks": [
        {
          "text": "Vellum",
          "start": 0.0,
          "duration": 1.4
        },
        {
          "text": "A river remembering a drawing.",
          "start": 1.58,
          "duration": 2.925
        },
        {
          "text": "Blue, green, and orange pigment move across warm paper, carried by currents that fold into eddies and gather around circular basins. A faint pencil construction gives the water something to follow, and something to escape. Concentrated colour passes into delicate, diluted traces.",
          "start": 4.685,
          "duration": 19.275
        },
        {
          "text": "Release ink, stir the water, or place an eddy. A gesture joins the same currents already moving through the sheet. Change the seed to begin another composition, or hold a moment and save it as a print.",
          "start": 24.14,
          "duration": 13.9
        },
        {
          "text": "The work explores the meeting of a drawn structure and a moving material. The surface holds their traces as the currents keep changing.",
          "start": 38.22,
          "duration": 9.275
        },
        {
          "text": "By Brad Necyk. Previously developed as Capillary. This living artwork is not inscribed.",
          "start": 47.675,
          "duration": 7.025
        }
      ],
      "checks": {
        "all_text_retained": true,
        "mp3_decodes": true,
        "finite_samples": true,
        "peak": 0.6225528717041016,
        "clipped_samples": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "fieldworks-primitives",
      "title": "Primitives",
      "form": "fieldwork",
      "release_id": null,
      "pages": [
        "primitives/"
      ],
      "source_path": "readings/primitives.md",
      "source_sha256": "eae6ef6edfd727ff35413936746d8c83d85f2c8f09276efb247555265c7ee839",
      "document_sha256": "eae6ef6edfd727ff35413936746d8c83d85f2c8f09276efb247555265c7ee839",
      "text_sha256": "50db3f60040f38e06010a154ebf1742657ea8bcca5d55c11c922f44b56d3b3bf",
      "reading_path": "audio/readings/50db3f60040f38e06010a154ebf1742657ea8bcca5d55c11c922f44b56d3b3bf.md",
      "reading_sha256": "eae6ef6edfd727ff35413936746d8c83d85f2c8f09276efb247555265c7ee839",
      "reading_length": 1030,
      "audio_path": "audio/lewis/50db3f60040f38e06010a154ebf1742657ea8bcca5d55c11c922f44b56d3b3bf.mp3",
      "voice": "bm_lewis",
      "voice_name": "Lewis",
      "speed": 1.0,
      "audio_sha256": "43420308175546ba8c9502ce80452f245432c3259d0d5a7a5b703a60e4d0fc36",
      "audio_length": 871532,
      "duration_seconds": 72.55,
      "chunks": [
        {
          "text": "Primitives",
          "start": 0.0,
          "duration": 1.575
        },
        {
          "text": "A small vocabulary, an expanding field.",
          "start": 1.755,
          "duration": 3.725
        },
        {
          "text": "Circles, crosses, rings, and repeated marks gather in a grid. Each shape is flat and translucent. Where the inks overlap, a darker colour appears. A complex design can be only two or three simple forms sharing the same center.",
          "start": 5.66,
          "duration": 16.325
        },
        {
          "text": "Constellation opens the work as a field of individual marks and small gatherings. Scroll or pinch to move between large shapes and a distant composition of fine, distinct cells. In Pattern lab, stepped islands gather, break into fragments, or dissolve into scattered cells. Empty space travels with the marks.",
          "start": 22.165,
          "duration": 21.075
        },
        {
          "text": "Cyber motion guides the view through smooth changes of scale while individual rows and columns shift one cell at a time. Pause to hold a composition, remix it, or save an image. Optional hand zoom lets you move through the field with two hands: apart for a wider view, together to approach. Hand tracking runs locally in your browser, and the camera starts only when you choose it.",
          "start": 43.42,
          "duration": 24.3
        },
        {
          "text": "By Brad Necyk. This living artwork is not inscribed.",
          "start": 67.9,
          "duration": 4.65
        }
      ],
      "checks": {
        "all_text_retained": true,
        "mp3_decodes": true,
        "finite_samples": true,
        "peak": 0.6462122797966003,
        "clipped_samples": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "fieldworks-opalia",
      "title": "Opalia",
      "form": "fieldwork",
      "release_id": null,
      "pages": [
        "opalia/"
      ],
      "source_path": "readings/opalia.md",
      "source_sha256": "59b4b23efaa88f8217808f020f16afbf97450996cb7762391510245cd8a3df8e",
      "document_sha256": "59b4b23efaa88f8217808f020f16afbf97450996cb7762391510245cd8a3df8e",
      "text_sha256": "e4d8f27321eebaa874731f1d54753e15fea88399cbd8b8f34ff3773fb2215e84",
      "reading_path": "audio/readings/e4d8f27321eebaa874731f1d54753e15fea88399cbd8b8f34ff3773fb2215e84.md",
      "reading_sha256": "59b4b23efaa88f8217808f020f16afbf97450996cb7762391510245cd8a3df8e",
      "reading_length": 699,
      "audio_path": "audio/lewis/e4d8f27321eebaa874731f1d54753e15fea88399cbd8b8f34ff3773fb2215e84.mp3",
      "voice": "bm_lewis",
      "voice_name": "Lewis",
      "speed": 1.0,
      "audio_sha256": "703ae63696fb8b946821b828108c94e9b862c6fbe2d9afa760784989074d096e",
      "audio_length": 620684,
      "duration_seconds": 51.645,
      "chunks": [
        {
          "text": "Opalia",
          "start": 0.0,
          "duration": 1.475
        },
        {
          "text": "A fold in seeing. Light, continually becoming.",
          "start": 1.655,
          "duration": 4.3
        },
        {
          "text": "Pearlescent waves pass through a continuous generative field. Their contours breathe while the colours separate, overlap, and return. Open Controls to change the rhythm, seed, spacing, contour, or iridescence, or leave the surface to unfold.",
          "start": 6.135,
          "duration": 16.7
        },
        {
          "text": "Opalia invites attention without a task. Repetition becomes a way of noticing difference, rather than a demand to arrive somewhere. Its relation to Cyberdelic OS lies in that encounter with perception and time. This is a curatorial reading, not a claim about consciousness or a physical simulation of light.",
          "start": 23.015,
          "duration": 21.5
        },
        {
          "text": "By Brad Necyk. Previously developed as Phase Loom. This living artwork is not inscribed.",
          "start": 44.695,
          "duration": 6.95
        }
      ],
      "checks": {
        "all_text_retained": true,
        "mp3_decodes": true,
        "finite_samples": true,
        "peak": 0.4907299280166626,
        "clipped_samples": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "fieldworks-undra",
      "title": "Undra",
      "form": "fieldwork",
      "release_id": null,
      "pages": [
        "undra/"
      ],
      "source_path": "readings/undra.md",
      "source_sha256": "8a89ec4cf907ce20c844c5eb127bb7fd7245f212511cf0e976f638d286a93626",
      "document_sha256": "8a89ec4cf907ce20c844c5eb127bb7fd7245f212511cf0e976f638d286a93626",
      "text_sha256": "b7b08420093958b70db94788d6cfbef9cd80a6c2d682de4380802aa56a8e429a",
      "reading_path": "audio/readings/b7b08420093958b70db94788d6cfbef9cd80a6c2d682de4380802aa56a8e429a.md",
      "reading_sha256": "8a89ec4cf907ce20c844c5eb127bb7fd7245f212511cf0e976f638d286a93626",
      "reading_length": 681,
      "audio_path": "audio/lewis/b7b08420093958b70db94788d6cfbef9cd80a6c2d682de4380802aa56a8e429a.mp3",
      "voice": "bm_lewis",
      "voice_name": "Lewis",
      "speed": 1.0,
      "audio_sha256": "6baf6f9fee43593616e59c1df234b6fab8bd00ba166244642e710d62f72f3db8",
      "audio_length": 612620,
      "duration_seconds": 50.97,
      "chunks": [
        {
          "text": "Undra",
          "start": 0.0,
          "duration": 1.525
        },
        {
          "text": "A living surface. A conversation with water.",
          "start": 1.705,
          "duration": 3.975
        },
        {
          "text": "Hold empty space to grow a droplet. Drag water together, let it gather, then separate it again. The field responds through a procedural model of fluid motion and light. Its forms are generated in the browser, not played from a film.",
          "start": 5.86,
          "duration": 16.325
        },
        {
          "text": "Undra offers a small experience of agency without complete control. Your gesture changes the conditions, and the material answers in its own way. This connection to Cyberdelic OS is a curatorial interpretation, not a claim that the artwork implements the whole operating system.",
          "start": 22.365,
          "duration": 19.575
        },
        {
          "text": "By Brad Necyk. Previously developed as Glop, also known as Water Droplet. This living artwork is not inscribed.",
          "start": 42.12,
          "duration": 8.85
        }
      ],
      "checks": {
        "all_text_retained": true,
        "mp3_decodes": true,
