      "audio_path": "audio/lewis/3a23035aa7aa13ebf7ff70cfaf29492ae16bc0e386167dda939a707be00fbbe8.mp3",
      "voice": "bm_lewis",
      "voice_name": "Lewis",
      "speed": 1.0,
      "audio_sha256": "2ca26467a1bf5c3e0df921a546d31e00f438a285da0594f0b7bd8bcab0838124",
      "audio_length": 684908,
      "duration_seconds": 57.0,
      "chunks": [
        {
          "text": "Soft Signal",
          "start": 0.0,
          "duration": 1.775
        },
        {
          "text": "A picture with weight.",
          "start": 1.955,
          "duration": 2.15
        },
        {
          "text": "An early computer dream fills the screen: a chrome sphere, a checkerboard, a lavender ribbon, a distant moon. Take hold anywhere and pull. The image gathers into silk, carrying its small world through every fold. Release it, and watch the surface find its way back to stillness.",
          "start": 4.285,
          "duration": 18.9
        },
        {
          "text": "Soft Signal begins with a newly generated image recalling the ray-traced landscapes of the early 1990s. It is an imagined memory of that visual language. The cloth responds to your gesture in the browser. Each lift, hesitation, and fall happens as you touch it.",
          "start": 23.365,
          "duration": 18.675
        },
        {
          "text": "A familiar screen becomes something briefly held. You can disturb the picture without losing it. Its return takes time.",
          "start": 42.22,
          "duration": 8.525
        },
        {
          "text": "By Brad Necyk, 2026. This living artwork is not inscribed.",
          "start": 50.925,
          "duration": 6.075
        }
      ],
      "checks": {
        "all_text_retained": true,
        "mp3_decodes": true,
        "finite_samples": true,
        "peak": 0.5571140646934509,
        "clipped_samples": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "fieldworks-of-three-musicians",
      "title": "Of Three Musicians",
      "form": "fieldwork",
      "release_id": null,
      "pages": [
        "of-three-musicians/"
      ],
      "source_path": "readings/of-three-musicians.md",
      "source_sha256": "a02c6a81bb7694cef70671dfae29a4adfffc715153efa065c464926454e3ea51",
      "document_sha256": "a02c6a81bb7694cef70671dfae29a4adfffc715153efa065c464926454e3ea51",
      "text_sha256": "3c01dab177c061bfa45f83a270e12280af197b3e48a63c8e68115a9613841eea",
      "reading_path": "audio/readings/3c01dab177c061bfa45f83a270e12280af197b3e48a63c8e68115a9613841eea.md",
      "reading_sha256": "a02c6a81bb7694cef70671dfae29a4adfffc715153efa065c464926454e3ea51",
      "reading_length": 915,
      "audio_path": "audio/lewis/3c01dab177c061bfa45f83a270e12280af197b3e48a63c8e68115a9613841eea.mp3",
      "voice": "bm_lewis",
      "voice_name": "Lewis",
      "speed": 1.0,
      "audio_sha256": "b6fab22ed45e69e5804238067fd925c4dfbda7803baffd7200135c9a35ca79ef",
      "audio_length": 792332,
      "duration_seconds": 65.95,
      "chunks": [
        {
          "text": "Of Three Musicians",
          "start": 0.0,
          "duration": 2.175
        },
        {
          "text": "A room that keeps trying to sing.",
          "start": 2.355,
          "duration": 2.7
        },
        {
          "text": "After Picasso, a Pierrot, a Harlequin, and a bearded musician gather in a little company of paper masks, angular instruments, and impossible profiles. Other players accompany them. A dog wanders below their chairs. The camera slips between bodies, hesitates, and leans too close to a playing hand.",
          "start": 5.235,
          "duration": 20.625
        },
        {
          "text": "The room is made in code and seen through a coarse field of red, green, and blue light. Its waltz is generated as it plays: a wavering machine voice, plucked chords, bass notes, dry clicks, and small, detuned bells. The same musical events move the fingers, strings, sticks, and keys.",
          "start": 26.04,
          "duration": 19.025
        },
        {
          "text": "Of Three Musicians brings the company of Picasso's painting into the uncertain time of an early computer trying to sing. The players keep their awkward commitments to the score. The dog belongs to another rhythm.",
          "start": 45.245,
          "duration": 14.45
        },
        {
          "text": "By Brad Necyk, 2026. This living artwork is not inscribed.",
          "start": 59.875,
          "duration": 6.075
        }
      ],
      "checks": {
        "all_text_retained": true,
        "mp3_decodes": true,
        "finite_samples": true,
        "peak": 0.5640038251876831,
        "clipped_samples": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "fieldworks-btc-swarm",
      "title": "BTC / SWARM",
      "form": "fieldwork",
      "release_id": null,
      "pages": [
        "btc-swarm/"
      ],
      "source_path": "readings/btc-swarm.md",
      "source_sha256": "262050e93efdc41118b4fef9454656405c0fbf527aa709dd617fc5f1978b6048",
      "document_sha256": "262050e93efdc41118b4fef9454656405c0fbf527aa709dd617fc5f1978b6048",
      "text_sha256": "ad650481814513b797fcb5022068fc1f23d6c4e8a029b8a09f8184612258f15d",
      "reading_path": "audio/readings/ad650481814513b797fcb5022068fc1f23d6c4e8a029b8a09f8184612258f15d.md",
      "reading_sha256": "262050e93efdc41118b4fef9454656405c0fbf527aa709dd617fc5f1978b6048",
      "reading_length": 1035,
      "audio_path": "audio/lewis/ad650481814513b797fcb5022068fc1f23d6c4e8a029b8a09f8184612258f15d.mp3",
      "voice": "bm_lewis",
      "voice_name": "Lewis",
      "speed": 1.0,
      "audio_sha256": "157394ba813d606050549c3d578d16d05b772b0b80fd02ed6c36176c4d287b62",
      "audio_length": 907820,
      "duration_seconds": 75.575,
      "chunks": [
        {
          "text": "BTC / SWARM",
          "start": 0.0,
          "duration": 2.325
        },
        {
          "text": "A history in formation.",
          "start": 2.505,
          "duration": 2.6
        },
        {
          "text": "Hundreds of cursors inhabit a black desktop. They open folders, move windows, copy passages, carry images, and reserve spaces for things that have not arrived. Behind their work, a website keeps assembling and scrolling. No single cursor holds the whole design.",
          "start": 5.285,
          "duration": 18.475
        },
        {
          "text": "The material is Bitcoin history: financial collapse, the white paper, a newspaper headline inside the genesis block, early exchanges, lost coins, arguments, institutions, and recurring dreams of a different kind of money. Archival photographs meet diagrams, verified bytes, and clearly labelled imagined scenes. Sources travel with the fragments. Uncertainty remains visible.",
          "start": 23.94,
          "duration": 25.225
        },
        {
          "text": "Open a folder. Drag a piece of the page. Gather the swarm and watch it break apart. The desktop is a fiction, but its coordination happens here, through local algorithms. Every seed produces another arrangement. The archive keeps becoming an interface, and the interface keeps becoming a draft.",
          "start": 49.345,
          "duration": 19.975
        },
        {
          "text": "By Brad Necyk, 2026. This living artwork is not inscribed.",
          "start": 69.5,
          "duration": 6.075
        }
      ],
      "checks": {
        "all_text_retained": true,
        "mp3_decodes": true,
        "finite_samples": true,
        "peak": 0.5640362501144409,
        "clipped_samples": 0
      }
    },
